{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1561597-caveats-and-charters","id":1561597,"title":"caveats and charters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-11T04:24:08-07:00","id":1561597,"title":"caveats and charters","content":"(English is not my first language i apologize if a give you an aneurysm)<br /> so I was reading through the core book recently and saw the flavour text on the Telekinesis spell which say's &quot;Mind over matter, movement through sheer will; a dozen cruder and lesser spells have been refined into the modern practice that allows action to occur at a distance&quot; which got me thinking that yes there should be a multitude of imperfect DIY spells running around, especially if were talking about sorcerers, so I came up with the system below to try and create what that would look like<br /> <br /> More than one way to skin a black tabby:<br /> curses aren't known for being clear cut affairs, they often have esoteric mind numbing laws attached to them intentional or otherwise, which by extension means that spells-the refined art of manipulating the very damnation affixed to an accursed-aren't going to be much different, and this yet presents another advantage to having good relations with your family and lineage, for generations families have accumulated entire archives of lore on their practices, access to that trove of arcane secrets gives one assurance that whatever spell they are to pick up is most likely going to do what you think it does and build upon it without it blowing up in your face, but accursed that give their families the cold shoulder or cut them completely aren't so lucky, a lot of the time they have to come up with their own spells or pick up whatever random scrap of lore they find that fit's their practices with little to no Tutelage, not to mention the possibility of someone scamming them with a spell that has a seemingly above average effect without mentioning it's many flaws, though it does give one the room to experiment with their magic and create tailor made affects that suit them limitation is the mother of innovation after all, and yet another reason why you should cut contact with a family is because an accursed taught a curriculum of clean curated spells will struggle to com up with new spells or even know that one can tinker a spell to such a wide extent, though families like the unburdened are kind of a sweet spot when it comes to this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Terms and conditions:<br /> at the moment you're about to learn a spell you can decide to take caveats for said spell, each caveat has a dot value running from 1 to 3, you get an amount of tokens equal to the combined dot value of each caveats you picked up with a maximum of 3 tokens, you may then spend said tokens on charters to enhance your spell.<br /> <br /> caveats:<br /> condition: the spell requires specific circumstances to function<br /> (\u2022):lenient but inconvenient conditions<br /> examples: requiring a sympathetic connection to the target either via a part of them a cherished object or just by touching them, the target must have spoken to the caster during this scene, the accursed must in some way announce that their going to cast the spell on the target.<br /> (\u2022\u2022):restrictive conditions<br /> examples: the spell only works during night or day, the target must have injured the caster during the scene, the caster must have a certain kind of object (bladed weapon, preserved remains, any kind of flower) on hand to be able to cast the spell.<br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022):highly restrictive conditions<br /> examples: the spell only works during dawn and dusk, the target must have vowed utter hatred toward the caster, the caster must have a very specific object on hand to cast the spell (their sires fang, the dress made by their partner, their families scared text)<br /> sacrifice: the spell requires a cost above and beyond the holding or bleeding of curse dice<br /> (\u2022)everyday sacrifices<br /> examples: a few paper bills, the life of an animal, a well cooked meal.<br /> (\u2022\u2022)loathed sacrifices<br /> examples: an injury and an appropriate physical status effect that can only be healed normally, a beloved object either the caster's or someone else's, revealing an embarrassing secret.<br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022)blasphemous sacrifices<br /> examples: the dramatic severing of a meaningful bond, the life of a human, an occult object.<br /> peril: the spell has a nasty side effect on the caster when used<br /> (\u2022)painful<br /> examples: broken fingers, having the caster's appearance warped for the rest of the scene, loss touch taste or smell.<br /> (\u2022\u2022)dangerous<br /> examples: mauled limb, invoke a torment without gaining curse dice or momentum, restricted behaviour until the end of the scene.<br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022)debilitating<br /> examples: punctured organs, risk damnation via a coin flip, loss of sight or hearing.<br /> complex: the spell is tricky and counter intuitive to cast<br /> for each dot add +1 difficulty to the spellcasting roll of the spell.<br /> wild: the spell seems to have a mind of it's own<br /> the spell suffers a complication with a level according to the dot rating, minor at (\u2022) moderate at (\u2022\u2022) and major at (\u2022\u2022\u2022), if not bought off the complication give's the storyteller the ability to twist the spells parameters and effect to an extant according to the severity of the complication.<br /> delayed: the spell take's a lot of time to cast<br /> (\u2022) three turns<br /> (\u2022\u2022) a scene<br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) a few hours<br /> limited: the caster can cast the spell a limited amount of times per session<br /> (\u2022) three times<br /> (\u2022\u2022) two times<br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) one time<br /> <br /> Charter:<br /> praxis: the spell is more easier to cast<br /> for each dot add +1 enhancement that stack to the spellcasting roll.<br /> cheap: sometimes an accursed need's a spell right fucking now<br /> for each dot reduce the amount of experience required to learn the spell.<br /> efficient: the spell requires less energy from the caster to use<br /> for each dot reduce the amount of curse dice that need to be bled or held to cast the spell to minimum of zero.<br /> mighty: the caster can more readily access the higher capabilities of the spell<br /> for each dot you may add +1 to your entanglement when it come's to buying advances for this spell<br /> (note: come up with more charters to make it an even 7 and 7 split between caveats and charters)<br /> <br /> Cleaning service:<br /> while modified spells can be strong they can be very annoying to deal with in the long run, which is why during appropriate narrative downtime an accursed can get rid of a caveat and with it any charter it contributed to, though if a charter was bought using tokens from multiple caveats each one must be given an appropriate amount of time before being disposed of (special: when it comes to the cheap charter the accursed must simply spend experience one for one to get rid of each dot of the caveat attached to the charter).<br /> <br /> Edges:<br /> (work in progress)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28967-springjackson","name":"SpringJackson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28967_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}